        "id": "attarieh2025",
        "title": "Attarieh, Nunes, Khani, Negahdar, Goli, Nazarirad, Nazarirad, Mojtahedi, Nosaka and Soori 2025, shoulder flexed versus extended elbow-flexion training: preacher versus Bayesian cable curls, regional hypertrophy and strength (Eur J Sport Sci 25(4):e12279; PMC11906226)",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11906226/"
      },
      {
        "id": "oliveira2009",
        "title": "Oliveira, Matta, Alves, Garcia and Vieira 2009, effect of the shoulder position on the biceps brachii EMG in different dumbbell curls (J Sports Sci Med 8(1):24-29; PMC3737788)",
        "url": "https://jssm.org/jssm-08-24.xml-abst"
      },
      {
        "id": "zabaleta2023",
        "title": "Zabaleta-Korta, Fernandez-Pena, Torres-Unda, Frances, Zubillaga and Santos-Concejero 2023, regional hypertrophy: exercises at long and short muscle lengths (preacher vs incline dumbbell curls) in trained women (J Hum Kinet 88:259-270; PMC10407320)",
        "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10407320"
      }
    ],
    "safety": {
      "cautions": [
        "Elbow or shoulder pain: lighten the dumbbell and shorten the range; stop if pain is sharp (clinical opinion).",
        "Keep the wrists straight (in line with the forearm); a bent-back wrist under load strains the forearm (clinical opinion).",
        "Pick the dumbbells up and set them down with a straight back and bent knees.",
        "Muscle glow colours and activation curves are illustrative, not measured EMG.",
        "Front-of-shoulder pain in the hanging position: use the incline curl instead (clinical opinion)."
      ],
      "modify": [
        "Shoulder discomfort: incline dumbbell curl.",
        "Elbow pain: neutral grip."
      ],
      "regressions": [
        "Incline dumbbell curl.",
        "Lighter dumbbells."
      ],
      "progressions": [
        "Slower lowering with a 1 s pause in the stretch."
      ]
    },
    "muscleNotes": {
      "biceps_r": "Main elbow flexor; lying on the bench with the arms hanging below it puts the shoulder in extension, which stretches the biceps long head at the start. Extended-shoulder and flexed-shoulder curls built the biceps similarly over 10 weeks (Attarieh 2025).",
      "biceps_l": "Main elbow flexor; lying on the bench with the arms hanging below it puts the shoulder in extension, which stretches the biceps long head at the start. Extended-shoulder and flexed-shoulder curls built the biceps similarly over 10 weeks (Attarieh 2025).",
      "forearm_extensors_r": "Brachioradialis (mapped to the forearm extensor region) assists elbow flexion, most with the forearm near neutral.",
      "forearm_extensors_l": "Brachioradialis (mapped to the forearm extensor region) assists elbow flexion, most with the forearm near neutral.",
      "forearm_flexors_r": "Wrist and finger flexors hold the handle and keep the wrist straight.",
      "forearm_flexors_l": "Wrist and finger flexors hold the handle and keep the wrist straight.",
      "ant_deltoid_r": "Holds the upper arm still in the stretched position below the bench.",
      "ant_deltoid_l": "Holds the upper arm still in the stretched position below the bench.",
      "core": "Keeps the trunk still so the hips do not swing the weight up.",
      "pec_r": "Steadies the arm in the hanging position with the front of the shoulder stretched.",
      "pec_l": "Steadies the arm in the hanging position with the front of the shoulder stretched."
    }
